---
description: >
  COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID
  
  1. Using old JWT format for anon key: Use sb_publishable_ prefix
  2. Missing required headers: Include Authorization, apikey, and X-Supabase-Api-Version
  3. Wrong phone format: Use +19729777432 not "+19729777432" in JSON
  4. Trying to use backend WebSocket: It's been removed, use Supabase Realtime
  5. Forgetting RLS is enabled: All frontend queries are filtered by user ID
  6. Using wrong database connection: Use Session Pooler (port 5432) not Direct (IPv6 incompatible)
  7. Not normalizing base URLs: Always strip trailing slashes to prevent double-slash bugs
  8. Not using prisma db push to sync database state.
  9. Not using prisma cli to access the database.
  10. Asking the user for information that you already have access too (through your tools) instead of grabbing the information yourself.
  11. Not outputting test results in markdown for readability.
  12. Planning to do research
  13. Not adding logs at each step of a new feature so that the feature can be debugged when it evitably works.
  14. Not removing the logs when putting the finishing touches on a feature.
  15. Returning back to the user without a passing test evaluation.
  16. Not checking if a server is running on a port already, and killing what exists there. 
  17. ASSUMING a server doesn't hot reload when it really does.
  18. Not knowing that if the user types SETUP they want u to start 5 terminal sessions, 
  - 1. one that starts /frontend via $ npm run dev, 
  - 2. one thats starts, /backend via $ npm run dev, 
  - 3. one that starts /agents via $ ./scripts/run_local_worker.sh
  - 3. one that is just primed to run $ npm run cleanup:all (cd to /backend)
  - 4. cd /mac-app
  - 5. cd /research
  - 19. Putting rules in the wrong folder or with the wrong extension—always use .cursor/rules/ for project-wide, <area>/.cursor/rules/ for area-specific, and .mdc extension with frontmatter.
  20. Adding unnecessary fallbacks instead of fixing the root issue—prefer simple, correct implementations (see rules.mdc).
  21. Not importing PrismaClient from the singleton
  22. Using absolute paths for assets (e.g., src="/image.png") in shared front-end code—these break in Electron (file:// protocol). Use CSS gradients, imported assets, or inline SVGs instead.


apply:
  when: always
---
